From 684831edfcb5b58278d26f950ad99ac6eb7edfdf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:54:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): the Recipes tab explains recipes, stars the stock
 material, derives Vc and fz
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

U11 of the tool library refit. The Recipes tab opens with one line
that says what a recipe is and which row operations take. A star
marks the row of the stock material in force (the setup stock's,
else the document's). Under the table, one line for each row gives
its surface speed and chip load; the lines are cached with their
input, so a still frame computes nothing. The buttons Add material…,
Suggest feeds and speeds and Copy recipes from tool… stand on one
row, with a units note. Each one writes the window's draft; the one
Apply lands it as one ChangeTool undo step.

Fixes #4337

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
